  "name": "Deinoss, The Twin of Chaos",
  "type": "deity",
  "effects": [],
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt\"><em>Category: Unseen Gods</em></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt\"><em>Primarily Practiced in: Worldwide, heavily in Zahnheim</em></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\">Espirian Domains: The Heavens (Paradia, Elysium, Baythal, Asphalus, Taranthara)</em></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt\">Deinoss promises an afterlife full of color and expression, in a realm teeming with the <em>joy de vivre, </em>where all can imagine and create freely for all time in their creator’s domain. His followers understand the concepts and philosophies behind cause and effect, understanding that change is measured, but also that expression of self is a form of imprinting oneself on life. He is popular among visionaries, artists, and bards.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt\"> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt\"><strong>Edicts</strong> Express through art, take risks and try something new, inspire others</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt\"><strong>Anathema</strong> Deny change, deny expression from self or from others</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong>Areas of Concern</strong></span><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"> Self-expression, change, freedom</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong>Religious Symbol</strong></span><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"> A branching river of multiple colors</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong>Sacred Animal</strong></span><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"> Deer</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong>Sacred Colors</strong></span><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"> white and pearl</span></p>"
